    "cornice": {
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "rule": "A full crowning cornice terminates the composition above a real, treatise-derived entablature -- part of the same continuous entablature the family kit already specifies runs above the order (renaissance-classical.kit.json).",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "classical-crowning-cornice",
          "status": "canonical"
        },
        {
          "id": "no-applied-cornice-corbelled-eave-only",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "CASCADE FIX. Inherited from mediterranean-vernacular via the real but weight-0.4 italian-villa-vernacular hybridizes_with lineage edge ('half its DNA is the Veneto agricultural building'), and wrong at the level it was wrongly applied: Palladian's own defining_characteristics headline is 'the temple front -- a pedimented portico of engaged or free-standing columns -- applied to a domestic building,' which requires a real crowning entablature and cornice. The vernacular's corbelled-eave logic correctly governs the barchesse farm wings (see column), not the classically-ordered principal block."
        }
      ],
      "note": "CASCADE FIX -- one of the most consequential in this batch. Palladian sits directly on the lineage chain that english-georgian and its descendants (tidewater-georgian, and per docs/inheritance.md's worked example the whole American Georgian branch) walk through, so an incorrect blanket 'no cornice' at this node would silently strip the crowning member from every downstream Georgian-family kit that does not independently re-specify it.",
      "sources": [
        "palladian.json defining_characteristics, proportion_packs[trim-classical]"
      ],
      "group": "envelope"
    },
